 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "9efb0092-3045-58e2-bed4-ca88fc8fe6c0"] :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5 \\\\ y=4t \\\\ z=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat would be the vector equation of the line?" :question/worked-solution "These parametric equations are equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4t \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-36023/ma-source-field/730c94540fda998a61add49bfec225b85399850b062506524c420c0b6c580ace"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
