 {:db/id "q-36778" :question/id #uuid "3b14bc23-f539-5c26-97da-0a4a4fc1772d" :question/math-academy-id "q-36778" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$E=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ -2 & -6\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $E-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nE-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 8 \\\\ -2 & -6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(E-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(E-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 8 \\\\ -2 & -6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(-6-\\lambda )-(-2)\\cdot 8 & =0 \\\\ -12-2\\lambda +6\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $E$ has only one eigenvalue $\\lambda =-2,$ which is a double root of the characteristic equation." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-36778/ma-source-field/ba1d503856a62d91afc620dd3a1d5d01ff0539dc0d368b9b1a332e92f990b648"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
