 {:db/id "q-36780/ma-source-field/de20334607b18cdaa8b26b67adc67b00c470ae50cbffb8fb78cee672cc769b4f" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c905a94-1e61-56fb-85f0-520ef6a3631a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-36780/ma-source-field/de20334607b18cdaa8b26b67adc67b00c470ae50cbffb8fb78cee672cc769b4f/e51c5b56414aeaf8b812864e4fee4cb5bf8fad22dab393d7bec93870d1f67215" "q-36780/ma-source-field/de20334607b18cdaa8b26b67adc67b00c470ae50cbffb8fb78cee672cc769b4f/8b5d455b58812a28e94eb5ccda863906f2ddfb259b3b80c9c6fef95452eece31" "q-36780/ma-source-field/de20334607b18cdaa8b26b67adc67b00c470ae50cbffb8fb78cee672cc769b4f/18d3ca60e1d07246082b95978447a5422c97d0e5eb27d8612a6677b026b6419a" "q-36780/ma-source-field/de20334607b18cdaa8b26b67adc67b00c470ae50cbffb8fb78cee672cc769b4f/e4ee14fbbfc611c19d6fe4b7b832c58c11238f1492d2f844cedbb7e4e7ddded1" "q-36780/ma-source-field/de20334607b18cdaa8b26b67adc67b00c470ae50cbffb8fb78cee672cc769b4f/bdb0c7f5d4b7fe04d9e602641d68ea6fc24fa542d5f2becc060b84154e0c0aca"] :answer-field/correct "q-36780/ma-source-field/de20334607b18cdaa8b26b67adc67b00c470ae50cbffb8fb78cee672cc769b4f/bdb0c7f5d4b7fe04d9e602641d68ea6fc24fa542d5f2becc060b84154e0c0aca" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-36780" :question/id #uuid "1fda33b2-0f78-5ef6-abce-da9e465c13f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-36780" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(P-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )(7-\\lambda )-1\\cdot (-5) & =0 \\\\ 49-7\\lambda -7\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+5 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-14\\lambda +54 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the discriminant of the quadratic equation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =(-14)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 54 \\\\  & =196-216 \\\\  & =-20 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the characteristic equation does not have real solutions and therefore $P$ does not have real eigenvalues." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-36780/ma-source-field/de20334607b18cdaa8b26b67adc67b00c470ae50cbffb8fb78cee672cc769b4f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
