 {:db/id "q-36905" :question/id #uuid "8cbc83e7-bc89-5609-b94a-0fe1dfb1bde0" :question/math-academy-id "q-36905" :question/problem "![](images/91/91f073fa77aab423ee33902451e61ad9f033b61b2a875b66ff69708d4361e24f.png)\n\nWhich of the graphs above correspond to an invertible function?" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible if and only if it's a one-to-one function. To determine which of the functions are one-to-one, we use the horizontal line test.\n\nFrom the above, we see that in each of the four given graphs, some horizontal lines intersect the curve more than once. Therefore, these are not one-to-one functions. As a result, none of them correspond to an invertible function." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-36905/ma-source-field/b8cceb0f118dc1aee27bce93011bce9caa88b5ba56a507990bd75f2802689dae"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
