 {:db/id "q-38108" :question/id #uuid "97a67cfa-cbb4-5ac8-9bbc-80fac24ef619" :question/math-academy-id "q-38108" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & x+4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{2}+0x+16} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{2}+4x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,4x-16}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,32\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$-term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+0x+16\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x-4 \\\\  & x+4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{2}+0x+16} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{2}+4x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,4x+16 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,4x-16}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ $x-4\\,$ and $\\,-4x+16.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-38108/ma-source-field/dfe3b1ce2e7f35b2026b3252b56aedd294e5b9c758608c9294b6cfbaccaef0df"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
