 {:db/id "q-38245/ma-source-field/65d3670243760fb1d4b534240e6efbf3a2a1de1ac05dd308b4af4628b0ccf63e" :answer-field/id #uuid "f05d1ca1-306f-5d0c-970a-e108a73f246e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-38245/ma-source-field/65d3670243760fb1d4b534240e6efbf3a2a1de1ac05dd308b4af4628b0ccf63e/4b85c8da3d1d8155e1df499739ff8a3382032635d2ff1e07a9ac753863a98b4b" "q-38245/ma-source-field/65d3670243760fb1d4b534240e6efbf3a2a1de1ac05dd308b4af4628b0ccf63e/bec3f5631aa3b5b1f8876d1263132d597cba431ecfe01fe4a15f343e70adb298" "q-38245/ma-source-field/65d3670243760fb1d4b534240e6efbf3a2a1de1ac05dd308b4af4628b0ccf63e/e1b532818463229bb500608a3e4285418160fd2535d0b46e02b49e216c8d64d7" "q-38245/ma-source-field/65d3670243760fb1d4b534240e6efbf3a2a1de1ac05dd308b4af4628b0ccf63e/2efbd31c9b8a4e1de3259c68fcef8e9c48ec8b437bf8dee82ce81ebc927dd606" "q-38245/ma-source-field/65d3670243760fb1d4b534240e6efbf3a2a1de1ac05dd308b4af4628b0ccf63e/5f9c095a730e36cd16a55a27c764f4ab3b6586403207e48e222e58770fae958d"] :answer-field/correct "q-38245/ma-source-field/65d3670243760fb1d4b534240e6efbf3a2a1de1ac05dd308b4af4628b0ccf63e/5f9c095a730e36cd16a55a27c764f4ab3b6586403207e48e222e58770fae958d" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-38245" :question/id #uuid "48feab89-768b-5b8e-8c0a-02f86fdff070" :question/math-academy-id "q-38245" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}+{v}^{2} \\\\ {u}^{2}-{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the locations of the critical points of $T,$ we need to solve \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)={u}^{2}+{v}^{2}$ and $y(u,v)={u}^{2}-{v}^{2}.$ \n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =2v \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =-2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2u & 2v \\\\ 2u & -2v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2u\\cdot (-2v)-2v\\cdot 2u \\\\  & =-4uv-4uv \\\\  & =-8uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =0 \\\\ -8uv & =0 \\\\ uv & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $uv=0$ defines the pair of intersecting lines $u=0$ and $v=0$ in the $uv$-plane. Notice that these lines correspond to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-38245/ma-source-field/65d3670243760fb1d4b534240e6efbf3a2a1de1ac05dd308b4af4628b0ccf63e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
