 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "f8683314-e1cb-5e62-aca4-60ca1e1c5bf9"] :question/problem "A skater is skating straight down a ramp. The displacement $D$ of the skater increases at a rate that's proportional to the square of the time $t,$ in seconds.\nWhat differential equation describes the rate of change of displacement $D$ at time $t,$ where $t$ is the time since he started skating?" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*A skater is skating straight down a ramp. The **displacement** $D$ of the skater **increases** at a **rate** that's **proportional** to the **square of the time** $t,$ in seconds. *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *displacement* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *square of the time.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}∝{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the displacement *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=k{t}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-38313/ma-source-field/375ed9a48100a6e43db4efae2deb7f9969c4fdb65a97e33497d4da4e98497efc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
 [:db/retract 17592186188919 :question/answer-fields 17592186187560]
 {:db/id "q-38324/ma-source-field/beb09f754a1f078400435491ebb4991d4c8db14843ece0287e16500067621f2b/22edaeafb339585de72fbdee1a8e51b200a342ad967c19947ad751f85945a784" :answer/id #uuid "ca0e9268-1caf-523c-b9f2-33b5e344e302" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=-kA+2,\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-38324/ma-source-field/beb09f754a1f078400435491ebb4991d4c8db14843ece0287e16500067621f2b/6ab0fd2d7f0be9fc1907b4cc9f3ae701a6f040e8e70315ff13376402d4b503f0" :answer/id #uuid "d5b05b1a-5684-5d7b-b75e-a7617a17e248" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=\\sqrt{kA}-2,\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}
