 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "0e1b36cf-56ef-56e7-80a1-3a4e3d34ad42"] :question/worked-solution "Let's call $P(x)$ the polynomial shown in the diagram.\n\nThe end behavior of $P(x)$ is\n\n- $P(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty ,$ and\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nConsequently, \n\n- the degree of $P(x)$ is odd, and\n\n- the leading coefficient of $P(x)$ is negative.\n\n- the $y$-intercept is negative, which means that $P(0)<0.$\n\nTherefore, of the given options, only $P(x)=-{x}^{3}+2x-1$ satisties all these conditions." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-38624/ma-source-field/ad6d263a874e03b96906eda2453c4eb22f948703bac8ab52358f4f53226318b7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
