 {:db/id "q-39709/ma-source-field/fb48903edb474bdc26811f7702f8f35a2c0f3bf6b5fc6b00e0751df31c53c24a" :answer-field/id #uuid "ec45c948-28d5-5ad6-a116-f2bf6a3a31b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-39709/ma-source-field/fb48903edb474bdc26811f7702f8f35a2c0f3bf6b5fc6b00e0751df31c53c24a/fd0d0d8126304a42286587bbe97c41ddf640159e3faf5bb32e576faf80c69af6" "q-39709/ma-source-field/fb48903edb474bdc26811f7702f8f35a2c0f3bf6b5fc6b00e0751df31c53c24a/0a129ca0900aba381a4812657a24aac604ebcecb17e26e563046b4b42e4fb692" "q-39709/ma-source-field/fb48903edb474bdc26811f7702f8f35a2c0f3bf6b5fc6b00e0751df31c53c24a/a2e4ce523c8f168c4d4b00dce5edf6c2011692b894766d60bd1295e51dfce26e" "q-39709/ma-source-field/fb48903edb474bdc26811f7702f8f35a2c0f3bf6b5fc6b00e0751df31c53c24a/c87fc999ae36fa5868f9d8bd8e29d1ded5fbb7347a467ab3772499705a5a3478" "q-39709/ma-source-field/fb48903edb474bdc26811f7702f8f35a2c0f3bf6b5fc6b00e0751df31c53c24a/30d710eb2e5d00ef9f99be6285328e769e0f3a6e290df28c34f308c0ba7fba39"] :answer-field/correct "q-39709/ma-source-field/fb48903edb474bdc26811f7702f8f35a2c0f3bf6b5fc6b00e0751df31c53c24a/0a129ca0900aba381a4812657a24aac604ebcecb17e26e563046b4b42e4fb692" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "ab44c8de-700d-51cc-ab4a-3755f7926aef"] :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}-v \\\\ {u}^{2}+v \\\\ {e}^{w}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)={u}^{2}-v,\\,y(u,v,w)={u}^{2}+v,\\,z(u,v,w)={e}^{w}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =-1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & ={e}^{w}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}2u & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2u & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {e}^{w}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={e}^{w}|\\begin{aligned}2u & -1 \\\\ 2u & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={e}^{w}(2u+2u) \\\\  & =4u{e}^{w}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ 4u{e}^{w} & =0 \\\\ u & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $u=0$ defines the plane $u=0,$ i.e., $vw$-plane." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-39709/ma-source-field/fb48903edb474bdc26811f7702f8f35a2c0f3bf6b5fc6b00e0751df31c53c24a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
