 {:db/id "q-40579" :question/id #uuid "ecdef7ff-1e8e-5448-88b3-81c3a4f39ef6" :question/math-academy-id "q-40579" :question/problem "Which of the following statements is true regarding the series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }0.12{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{3n}$ ?" :question/worked-solution "The series starts with $n=1.$ So the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.12{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{3(2)}}{0.12{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{3(1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{6}}{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{3}} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3}{2})}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is divergent because $|r|\\ge 1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-40579/ma-source-field/0d2bfebf3f0b94b724349ff4922ba11f49b5315634b19eb267c6ab1e33ea0652"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
